| `if (!emailResult.success) emailError = …` → `void emailResult` (H1) | RED — k106 "a resolved send failure is recorded and reported, not read as success": `expected { status: 201, rowsPersisted: 1, …} to deeply equal {…}` (`emailSent: true, emailError: undefined`) |
| `if (opened) await client.query('ROLLBACK')` → unconditional (L1) | RED — `expected [ …(2) ] to not include 'ROLLBACK'` at the admin-client assertion |
| `withErrorHandler(withInviteToken(handler))` → `withInviteToken(handler)` on accept.ts (L7) | RED — `Error: disposable gotrue outage` escapes the handler again |
| `log.info(…, { inviteId: inv.id, … })` → `{ token, … }` (L6) | RED — `expected '[["Invitation accepted via token page…' not to contain 'k041l000…'` |
| `/register` reads `router.query.signup === '1'` instead of the server verdict (L3) | RED — "ignores ?signup=1 on a token the accept flow can complete" |

